{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-485899-r4673515","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Telur Dadar","sourcePageId":485899,"sourceRevision":"4673515","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-10-01T18:23:33Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Telur%20Dadar&oldid=4673515","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:11.956Z","sourceCategories":[],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e1794bd4d47326fc0c9cb699c5873184466164cff48cb718331324005fd563f1","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Cuisine = Indonesian\n| Origin = \n| Servings = 3–4\n| Time = 10 minutes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}| [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Indonesia|Cuisine of Indonesia]]\n\n'''Telur dadar''' is an Indonesian dish made of eggs with some herbs and additional ingredients, with the word ''dadar'' referring to the method of spreading the egg mixture during cooking. This dish is better served with warm rice.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 2–3 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Ground pepper]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Dehydrated Broth|chicken stock powder]]\n* 1 clove [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Green Onion|spring onion]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 1 stalk [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]] (optional), chopped\n* 1–2 [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]] (optional), chopped\n* ½ can [[Cookbook:Corned Beef|corned beef]]\n* 1 sliced [[Cookbook:Tofu|tofu]] (optional)\n* [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|Cooking oil]]\n* [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|Soy sauce]] for serving (optional)\n* Fried [[Cookbook:Shallot|shallots]] (optional)\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# [[Cookbook:Beat|Beat]] the eggs, salt, pepper, and stock powder together in a bowl until well-combined.\n# Mix in the garlic, spring onion, celery, and chile.\n# Scoop the corned beef into the mixture, then use a spoon to break it into smaller pieces before mixing well again.\n# Add the tofu, but do not mix, as this would crush the soft tofu.\n# Heat a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|skillet]] over medium heat. Add a thin coat of oil, then spread the egg mixture evenly in the pan.\n# Let the egg cook until fully cooked on the bottom, then flip the egg and cook the other side until done.\n# Serve on a plate with soy sauce and fried shallots as desired.\n[[Category:Very Easy recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes]]\n[[Category:Indonesian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corned beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tofu]]\n[[Category:Recipes using soy sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using shallot]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Telur Dadar","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"3–4","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2–3 eggs","sourceText":"2–3 eggs","amountText":"2–3 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 tsp salt","sourceText":"1 tsp salt","amountText":"1 tsp salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Ground 